<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chile</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Republic of Chile</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chile is a country in the Southern Cone of southwestern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, a narrow strip of land between the Andes Mountains and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> conquered and colonized the region in the mid-16th century, replacing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> rule, but failed to conquer the autonomous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> people of what is now south-central Chile. Chile declared independence from Spain in 1818. It ended Mapuche resistance in the 1880s and gained its present northern territory by defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-pacific">War of the Pacific</a> (1879–83). The coup of 11 September 1973 overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador-allende">Salvador Allende</a> and began a military <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-pinochet">Augusto Pinochet</a> that lasted until 1990.</p></div>
